{"parentUuid":"456ca50d-1f81-4214-85eb-f4c32a738878","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyKtgT9ASLU5NrN9Rzc5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332,"cache_read_input_tokens":696044,"output_tokens":975,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":975,"cache_read_input_tokens":696044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"aada12c0-43c4-40d7-aad8-1f6d5ccd9216","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgyKtfy7P4Ts54X7qer88","type":"assistant","uuid":"28ecd0a4-964a-4dd4-b5e3-c661d95b226b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:11:01.501Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"28ecd0a4-964a-4dd4-b5e3-c661d95b226b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyKtgT9ASLU5NrN9Rzc5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both pages are gone. Constraints and capabilities now live with the workflow steps, grouped by charter, harness and factory, and each row keeps its promote and demote. There are three commits, `3f3657e`, `f99997d` and `ddbaaef`. CI and the safeguard pass, and I checked each part in the app. Nothing is pushed.\n\n**A step's Rules tab** (replaces the Constraints and Capabilities tabs):\n- **Charter:** each workspace's repository rules and hooks, read-only, with \"Change it there.\"\n- **Harness:** the step's grants (its own, or its kind's), then the rules and hooks on calls.\n- **Factory:** the review checks and the reviewers.\n- **Rung switch:** each constraint has a Told | Checked | Enforced switch, and each grant has Ask | Allowed. Clicking a rung moves it there. A new call, `PUT /constraints/{id}/rung`, moves one rung at a time, so the audit still records each promotion and demotion.\n- **Add bar:** a grant, a rule, a hook, a reviewer, or a constraint from another step.\n\n**The every-step panel** shows when you pick no step on the Workflows page:\n- the charters;\n- the grants for Prompt, Agent and Skill steps;\n- the rules and hooks for every step;\n- the review checks;\n- the factory's three fixed rows (merge, network, send back), read-only.\n\nAn admin adds a grant for one kind there, or a rule, hook or reviewer for every step.\n\n**Docs:** `VISION.md` says where rules live now, and `DECISIONS.md` has D53. The Audit Log keeps each rule's history, which the old page showed inline.\n\n**Decisions I made that you may want to change:**\n- **No one-click delete for seeded rules.** In the every-step panel, Remove shows only on constraints made from the app (ids `rule-`, `hook-`, `reviewer-`). A seeded rule such as \"Commit no secret\" can only be moved down its rungs.\n- **Kind grants still have Remove.** Removing the Prompt kind's `sandbox::*` would refuse every call at every prompt step, and it takes one click with no confirmation.\n- **The shell kind's grant isn't shown.** A `shell` kind grant of `sandbox::*` exists, but a shell step runs no agent, so the panel leaves it out.\n\n**One correction:** while testing yesterday, a misplaced click gave Bug fix's build step its own `sandbox::*` grant. It matched the kind's grant, so jobs ran the same. The audit shows it, and I removed it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332,"cache_read_input_tokens":696044,"output_tokens":975,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":975,"cache_read_input_tokens":696044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"aada12c0-43c4-40d7-aad8-1f6d5ccd9216","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyKtfy7P4Ts54X7qer88","type":"assistant","uuid":"010d33c0-2950-4f22-89dd-ff8030d5e79f","timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:11:02.534Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
