tep, and\n  `!` before any of them for off.\n- At a step, its own setting wins, then its workflow's, then the all\n  workflows setting. A list with no `*` keeps today's meaning: on at every\n  step when it names no step to turn on, and on only where it says\n  otherwise.\n- A grant is an item for one kind and one function, with its rung. A\n  step's own grants no longer replace its kind's: a step turns items on or\n  off. The gate folds the few step grants from before into items once.\n- `PUT /scopes` sets an item's setting at a scope: on, off, or inherit.\n\n### G2. Levels on the Workflows page\n\n- A level bar: All workflows › the workflow › the step. Picking a step on\n  the canvas opens its level, and the canvas background opens the\n  workflow's.\n- Each level shows the same Rules view: the charter, the harness and the\n  factory. Each item has an Inherit | On | Off switch, says what it\n  inherits, and keeps its rung switch.\n- The Add bar adds an item on at the level it is on.\n\n### G3. One rule, two forms (D55)\n\n- A constraint shows how it is judged: by an agent (told, or a reviewer)\n  or by code (a word match, a hook, or a review check).\n- Promoting a told rule asks for its deterministic form: the words a call\n  holds, or a hook command. Demoting keeps that form and stops running it.\n- A grant's rung stays ask or allowed.\n\n'''\ns=head+s[i:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| D53 |'); j=s.index('\\n',i)+1\ns=s[:j]+'''| D54 | A constraint or a grant is one item that three scopes turn on or off: all workflows (`*`), one workflow, and one step, each with `!` for off. The most specific setting wins. A list with no `*` means every step when it turns no step on, and only the steps it names otherwise. A grant is an item for one kind and one function; a step turns items on or off rather than replacing its kind's grants, which replaces D48's \"take the place of\". A rung belongs to the item, not to a scope. |\n| D55 | A constraint is judged by an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or by code (a word match, a hook, a review check). Promoting a told rule gives it a deterministic form; demoting keeps the form and stops running it. |\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py PLAN.md 2>&1 | head -5","description":"Write the scopes plan and D54, D55"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Qpe6o8pbtqvmeARBRKK4px":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ea9da6c7-6adc-4c95-b38e-fd29e0d97dc2","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgyPZ7EZSbX2dxp3Buk3T","type":"assistant","uuid":"c19dc2ce-0d4b-4c92-8742-1c9985cfa2e1","timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:59:27.311Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
