{"parentUuid":"c19dc2ce-0d4b-4c92-8742-1c9985cfa2e1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b9900b6a-4bcb-43a2-b19b-738de97bb619","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qpe6o8pbtqvmeARBRKK4px","type":"tool_result","content":"PLAN [informational/ste]  (491 words, 3 findings)\n  - reader address low: 0.0/1k words (\"you\" plus imperatives, floor 8.0); page lectures instead of helps\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it\n  - passive voice: 4.8% of sentences (max 3.0%); name the actor [heuristic: verify each hit]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"750a6d9e-e2ed-4a61-8131-068507b7d678","timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:59:27.736Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"PLAN [informational/ste]  (491 words, 3 findings)\n  - reader address low: 0.0/1k words (\"you\" plus imperatives, floor 8.0); page lectures instead of helps\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it\n  - passive voice: 4.8% of sentences (max 3.0%); name the actor [heuristic: verify each hit]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":80,"oldLines":6,"newStart":80,"newLines":8,"lines":[" | D51 | A constraint may name a reviewer from `.agents/agents/`. When its step finishes, the reviewer reads the step's change in a turn with no tools, from its file at the job's base, and its fail fails the step as D47 says. A reviewer that can't run leaves the job with a person. |"," | D52 | A server's MCP servers reach a turn through `workers/bastion-mcp`, which registers each tool as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`. Only MCP servers over HTTP: a stdio server would run on the host, outside the VM. A server's token stays in the vault, and only the bridge may read it. |"," | D53 | A step's rules live with the step, on the Workflows page, in one tab by layer: the charter (read-only, from the repository), the harness (grants, and the rules and hooks on calls), and the factory (review checks and reviewers). With no step picked, the page shows what applies at every step. Each rung is a switch. There is no Constraints or Capabilities page. |","+| D54 | A constraint or a grant is one item that three scopes turn on or off: all workflows (`*`), one workflow, and one step, each with `!` for off. The most specific setting wins. A list with no `*` means every step when it turns no step on, and only the steps it names otherwise. A grant is an item for one kind and one function; a step turns items on or off rather than replacing its kind's grants, which replaces D48's \"take the place of\". A rung belongs to the item, not to a scope. |","+| D55 | A constraint is judged by an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or by code (a word match, a hook, a review check). Promoting a told rule gives it a deterministic form; demoting keeps the form and stops running it. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":113,"newStart":1,"newLines":55,"lines":["-# Bastion plan: more a step may do, more that checks it","+# Bastion plan: rules at three scopes, in two forms"," "," <!-- voice-register: informational -->"," <!-- voice-english: ste -->"," ","-A step's capabilities grow past iii functions. It may run named shell","-commands, call more tools, and reach MCP servers. Its constraints grow past","-rules: hooks run before its calls, and a reviewer agent must pass its change","-before the job moves on. The cost is reach. Each new capability is a new","-way for an agent to act, so each one starts ungranted and the gate decides","-every call, the same as today.","+A constraint or a grant is one item, and three scopes turn it on or off:","+all workflows, one workflow, and one step. The most specific setting wins,","+so a rule can be on for all workflows, off for one workflow, and on again","+at one of its steps. A rule also has two forms. An agent judges a told rule","+or a reviewer's verdict; code judges a word match, a hook, or a review","+check. Promoting a rule moves it from the first form to the second. The","+cost is reading: each row now says where its setting comes from."," ","-The top-bar plan (U1 to U13) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions","-are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D49 to D52.","+The capabilities plan (C1 to C4) is done, and git history holds it.","+Decisions are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 and D55."," "," ## Phases"," "," Each phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit"," before the next one starts."," ","-### C1. Named commands and more tools (D49)","-","-- A grant on `sandbox::exec` may name a command after the function:","-  `sandbox::exec cargo test`. That grant covers a call only when the","-  command line starts with those words.","-- A grant that names a command never covers a line with shell operators","-  (`;`, `&&`, `|`, `` ` ``, `$(`, `>`), because the operators would run a","-  second command. A grant that names no command still covers every line.","-- The most specific grant decides, as today: a named command wins over","-  plain `sandbox::exec`.","-- A turn's `functions.allow` is the four sandbox tools plus every function","-  its step's grants name. Today it is the four tools only, so a grant on","-  any other function can never be called.","-- The step editor's grant form takes the command words after the","-  function. The command lives in the grant's function, so the store and","-  the API don't change.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live, on Short's plan step with its own grants","-`sandbox::fs::*` and `sandbox::exec git`: `git -C /work/repo log","---oneline -3` ran, and `ls -la /work/repo` was refused with \"No grant","-covers sandbox::exec at short/plan.\" The four sandbox tools are in every","-turn's list by name, so this did not show whether the harness takes a","-pattern such as `sandbox::*`. C4 settled it: a grant on `mcp::calc::*` was","-the only thing naming the MCP tool, and the turn called it.","-","-### C2. Hooks per step (D50)","-","-- A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before","-  each matching call at its steps. Exit 2 refuses the call, and its output","-  is the reason.","-- The charter's `PreToolUse` hooks still run. A step's hooks run after","-  them.","-- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook. A","-  hook that is only told doesn't run, and only an owner's constraint can","-  be removed: a charter's changes in its repository.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live, a hook at Short's plan step that exits 2: the turn's","-`git log` was refused with \"A hook refused this call: hook says no\", and","-the audit kept the hook's run. In the app, Bug fix's build step added","-`./.agents/hooks/check.sh` as a hook and removed it again; the audit","-recorded both.","-","-### C3. A reviewer that must pass (D51)","-","-- A constraint may name a reviewer: an agent in `.agents/agents/`. When","-  its step finishes, Bastion runs one turn as that agent on the step's","-  change.","-- The reviewer answers pass or fail with its reasons. A fail fails the","-  step, so the job goes along the failure link or back to the fixer, as","-  D47 says. The step's revisions bound the loop.","-- The reviewer's turn has no tools: it reads its agent file as the job's","-  base has it, the request, and the change, on the server's plan model. A","-  turn under review can't rewrite its reviewer.","-- Its reply is an artifact on the step, and its cost counts toward the","-  step's budget. A reviewer that can't run, or gives no verdict, leaves","-  the job with a person.","-- The step editor adds a reviewer and removes one made for that step.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live, a `strict` agent that fails every change, on Short's","-plan step: the job waited with \"The reviewer strict failed it\", and the","-review was kept as \"Review by strict\". A plan step only reads, so a fail","-there has no step to go back to and waits for a person. In the app, Bug","-fix's build step added `strict` as a reviewer and removed it.","-","-### C4. MCP servers (D52)","-","-- iii ships no MCP bridge; its docs say to write a worker that bridges MCP","-  into `trigger()` calls. `workers/bastion-mcp` is that worker, in Rust","-  (D6).","-- A server lists its MCP servers in Settings: a name, a URL, and the name","-  of the secret that holds its token, if it needs one.","-- The bridge registers each tool of a server as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`.","-  A step's grant on `mcp::github::*` lets its agent call that server's","-  tools, and C1 puts them in the turn's `functions.allow`.","-- Only MCP servers that answer over HTTP, this round. A stdio server runs","-  as a process on the host, outside the VM, and VISION.md says agent work","-  never runs on your machine.","-- A server's token stays in the vault. Settings names the secret, and the","-  server makes `bastion-mcp` a consumer of it, so only the bridge reads it.","-- The gate's hook now binds every function a turn calls, not only","-  `sandbox::*`. Since C1 a turn may call any function its step grants, and","-  a call the hook doesn't bind skips the gate.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live, a test MCP server with one tool, `add`, listed as","-`calc`: the bridge said \"connected, 1 tools\", and a job whose plan step was","-granted `mcp::calc::*` called `mcp::calc::add` with 2 and 3 and got 5. The","-first run showed no gate entry for that call: the hook bound only","-`sandbox::*`. With the hook on every function, the audit shows \"continue","-mcp::calc::add\" and the sandbox calls as before. Removing `calc` in","-Settings took its tool off the engine.","+### G1. Scopes in the core and the server (D54)","+","+- A constraint's and a grant's scope list holds settings: `*` for all","+  workflows, `bug-fix` for one workflow, `bug-fix/build` for one step, and","+  `!` before any of them for off.","+- At a step, its own setting wins, then its workflow's, then the all","+  workflows setting. A list with no `*` keeps today's meaning: on at every","+  step when it names no step to turn on, and on only where it says","+  otherwise.","+- A grant is an item for one kind and one function, with its rung. A","+  step's own grants no longer replace its kind's: a step turns items on or","+  off. The gate folds the few step grants from before into items once.","+- `PUT /scopes` sets an item's setting at a scope: on, off, or inherit.","+","+### G2. Levels on the Workflows page","+","+- A level bar: All workflows › the workflow › the step. Picking a step on","+  the canvas opens its level, and the canvas background opens the","+  workflow's.","+- Each level shows the same Rules view: the charter, the harness and the","+  factory. Each item has an Inherit | On | Off switch, says what it","+  inherits, and keeps its rung switch.","+- The Add bar adds an item on at the level it is on.","+","+### G3. One rule, two forms (D55)","+","+- A constraint shows how it is judged: by an agent (told, or a reviewer)","+  or by code (a word match, a hook, or a review check).","+- Promoting a told rule asks for its deterministic form: the words a call","+  holds, or a hook command. Demoting keeps that form and stops running it.","+- A grant's rung stays ask or allowed."," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ea9da6c7-6adc-4c95-b38e-fd29e0d97dc2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c19dc2ce-0d4b-4c92-8742-1c9985cfa2e1","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
