{"parentUuid":"7b9779c8-0608-4ae6-b382-9067294f99af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyQZ9BkDKH9eXMfH3v3m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The three scopes work. A rule or grant can now be on or off for all workflows, for one workflow, and for one step, and the most specific setting wins. There are two commits, `dbc3f40` and `d7db219`. CI and the safeguard pass, and nothing is pushed.\n\n**How it works (D54):**\n- Each constraint and grant is one item, with one rung (told, checked, enforced; or ask, allowed).\n- At each level it is Inherit, On or Off. A step's setting wins over its workflow's, which wins over all workflows.\n- A step no longer replaces its kind's grants (that was D48). It turns items on or off instead.\n- The gate folded the one old step grant (`bug-fix/plan`'s `sandbox::*`) into an item once. The jobs that step runs see the same grants, and the audit records the fold.\n\n**The Workflows page:**\n- A level bar reads All workflows › Bug fix › build.\n- Click a step on the canvas for its level, the canvas background for the workflow's, or \"All workflows\" for the top. The canvas hides at All workflows.\n- Every level shows the same layers: Charter (read-only), Harness and Factory.\n- Each row has its rung switch, then a \"here\" switch: Inherit · on/off, On, Off. A row that is off at this level shows in gray.\n- The Add bar adds an item that is on at the level you're on.\n- Remove deletes an item everywhere, so it only shows at All workflows.\n\n**Live check:** I turned \"Keep shell use small\" Off for Bug fix. The build step then showed \"Inherit · off\", and turning it On there gave `* !bug-fix bug-fix/build`. Then I set both back to inherit.\n\n**Your rule-or-hook idea:** you said promote and demote could also move a rule between an inferential form (a told rule, a reviewer) and a deterministic one (a word match, a hook, a review check). I've planned that as G3 (D55): promoting a told rule asks for its deterministic form, and demoting keeps that form and stops running it. I haven't built it yet. The new levels are a big UI change, and I'd like you to look at them first. Should I go ahead with G3 as planned?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":727,"cache_read_input_tokens":820213,"output_tokens":860,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":149},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":727,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":860,"cache_read_input_tokens":820213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":727},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"db026bd6-0eb9-4c45-bf67-52e4f4d19ccf","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyQZ8dGaqzwxQajRd9dR","type":"assistant","uuid":"39770db4-f514-4d12-8989-a50289142e75","timestamp":"2026-11-12T17:12:11.957Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
