{"parentUuid":"2380c06c-8c2c-4331-9a16-4bbc8a91cbc3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"37211818-95a6-4835-b720-c9efefd2895a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017s6Gc1iGV6tJWoZ91tXmBn","type":"tool_result","content":"PLAN [informational/ste]  (402 words, 4 findings)\n  - reader address low: 5.0/1k words (\"you\" plus imperatives, floor 8.0); page lectures instead of helps\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ba5074bb-8a3f-4aef-87a8-f2e6eec33262","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:37:40.603Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"PLAN [informational/ste]  (402 words, 4 findings)\n  - reader address low: 5.0/1k words (\"you\" plus imperatives, floor 8.0); page lectures instead of helps\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":82,"oldLines":6,"newStart":82,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D53 | A step's rules live with the step, on the Workflows page, in one tab by layer: the charter (read-only, from the repository), the harness (grants, and the rules and hooks on calls), and the factory (review checks and reviewers). With no step picked, the page shows what applies at every step. Each rung is a switch. There is no Constraints or Capabilities page. |"," | D54 | A constraint or a grant is one item that three scopes turn on or off: all workflows (`*`), one workflow, and one step, each with `!` for off. The most specific setting wins. A list with no `*` means every step when it turns no step on, and only the steps it names otherwise. A grant is an item for one kind and one function; a step turns items on or off rather than replacing its kind's grants, which replaces D48's \"take the place of\". A rung belongs to the item, not to a scope. |"," | D55 | A constraint is judged by an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or by code (a word match, a hook, a review check). Promoting a told rule gives it a deterministic form; demoting keeps the form and stops running it. |","+| D56 | A constraint or capability is inferential, which an agent judges, or deterministic, which code decides; it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: an inferential constraint is said to the agent, a deterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. An inferential capability is a skill, an agent, or a note on what the agent may do. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":73,"newStart":1,"newLines":51,"lines":["-# Bastion plan: rules at three scopes, in two forms","+# Bastion plan: rules by who judges them"," "," <!-- voice-register: informational -->"," <!-- voice-english: ste -->"," ","-A constraint or a grant is one item, and three scopes turn it on or off:","-all workflows, one workflow, and one step. The most specific setting wins,","-so a rule can be on for all workflows, off for one workflow, and on again","-at one of its steps. A rule also has two forms. An agent judges a told rule","-or a reviewer's verdict; code judges a word match, a hook, or a review","-check. Promoting a rule moves it from the first form to the second. The","-cost is reading: each row now says where its setting comes from.","+A step's rules sort on three questions. Is it a constraint or a","+capability? Does an agent judge it (inferential) or code (deterministic)?","+And does it come from the workspace's repository or from Bastion? Each","+item is on or off at a step, or for every step of its workflow. Told,","+checked and enforced go: an inferential rule is said to the agent, a","+deterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. The","+cost is the old \"checked\" rules, which noted a break and let it pass;","+they start off, so nothing changes until you turn one on."," ","-The capabilities plan (C1 to C4) is done, and git history holds it.","-Decisions are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 and D55.","+The scopes plan (G1 to G3) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions","+are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 to D56."," "," ## Phases"," "," Each phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit"," before the next one starts."," ","-### G1. Scopes in the core and the server (D54)","+### R1. The model on the server (D56)"," ","-- A constraint's and a grant's scope list holds settings: `*` for all","-  workflows, `bug-fix` for one workflow, `bug-fix/build` for one step, and","-  `!` before any of them for off.","-- At a step, its own setting wins, then its workflow's, then the all","-  workflows setting. A list with no `*` keeps today's meaning: on at every","-  step when it names no step to turn on, and on only where it says","-  otherwise.","-- A grant is an item for one kind and one function, with its rung. A","-  step's own grants no longer replace its kind's: a step turns items on or","-  off. The gate folds the few step grants from before into items once.","-- `PUT /scopes` sets an item's setting at a scope: on, off, or inherit.","+- A constraint's mode is inferential (stored as told) or deterministic","+  (stored as enforced). Migration 9 turns each checked one deterministic","+  and off for every workflow.","+- A constraint row may be a capability: a note told to the agent as what","+  it may do, such as a skill to use. The brief lists them under \"You may\".","+- The charter listing adds the repository's skills and agents, which a","+  workspace brings as inferential capabilities.","+- Setting a mode refuses checked."," ","-Done 2026-11-12. Live, the gate folded the one step grant from before,","-Bug fix's plan step's `sandbox::*`, into the prompt kind's item as","-`* bug-fix/plan`, and the audit kept the fold. `PUT /scopes` turned \"Keep","-shell use small\" off for Bug fix, as `* !bug-fix`, and back to inherit.","+### R2. The rules view by type and mode"," ","-### G2. Levels on the Workflows page","+- Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into","+  inferential and deterministic, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every","+  row.","+- A Bastion constraint has an Inferential | Deterministic switch; going","+  deterministic asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask |","+  Allowed.","+- The levels are the workflow and the step. What applies to every","+  workflow shows as inherited at the workflow; editing it for all","+  workflows waits."," ","-- A level bar: All workflows › the workflow › the step. Picking a step on","-  the canvas opens its level, and the canvas background opens the","-  workflow's.","-- Each level shows the same Rules view: the charter, the harness and the","-  factory. Each item has an Inherit | On | Off switch, says what it","-  inherits, and keeps its rung switch.","-- The Add bar adds an item on at the level it is on.","+### R3. Docs"," ","-Done 2026-11-12. Live, at Bug fix \"Keep shell use small\" went Off, as","-`* !bug-fix`; Bug fix's build step then showed it as \"Inherit · off\", and","-On there gave `* !bug-fix bug-fix/build`. At All workflows the canvas","-hides and each item shows On | Off, with Remove. A \"here\" label sets the","-scope switch apart from the rung switch beside it.","-","-### G3. One rule, two forms (D55)","-","-- A constraint shows who judges it: an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or","-  code (a word match, a hook, or a review check).","-- Promoting a told rule asks for its deterministic form: the words a call","-  holds, or a hook command. Demoting keeps that form and stops running it.","-- A grant's rung stays ask or allowed.","-- \"Form\" on a rule edits that form at any rung.","-","-Done 2026-11-12. Live, at All workflows a told test rule showed \"agent","-judges it\". Enforced opened its form, which asked for calls to match or a","-hook; with `./.agents/hooks/lint.sh` it saved as an enforced hook, \"code","-judges it\". Told then kept the hook and stopped it running. The audit kept","-the form, both promotions, and both demotions.","+- VISION.md and DECISIONS.md say how rules sort."," "," ## Open questions"," "]},{"oldStart":76,"oldLines":3,"newStart":54,"newLines":5,"lines":["   one?"," - **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use","   a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?","+- **Rules for every workflow.** Whether some items should be set once for","+  all workflows, and where that lives."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b8edb6d7-ea22-4f33-b62d-90937acbd048","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2380c06c-8c2c-4331-9a16-4bbc8a91cbc3","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
