{"parentUuid":"30292af7-968e-41da-ae36-0b8ccfec6cab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgybjgE6nmGvMVLyLBA2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The mapping is done except for reviewers, which I'd put under feedback since a reviewer agent judges the change after it runs; the R1 build passed, and I'm updating the plan and D56 next. Tell me if you'd rather have reviewers under feedforward.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3581,"cache_read_input_tokens":874195,"output_tokens":1860,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":571},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3581,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1860,"cache_read_input_tokens":874195,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3581},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"52d14907-8b07-4eb2-a498-44b02ba2ffb9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgybjfpZDxnpsAf56Hf6e","type":"assistant","uuid":"441f60a3-207b-4a14-9d6f-f622a1217bef","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:38:47.923Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"441f60a3-207b-4a14-9d6f-f622a1217bef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgybjgE6nmGvMVLyLBA2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RgDjmir3yRjX8fvfLfLJgE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('### R2.')\nhead=s[:i]\nhead=head.replace('''A step's rules sort on three questions. Is it a constraint or a\ncapability? Does an agent judge it (inferential) or code (deterministic)?\nAnd does it come from the workspace's repository or from Bastion? Each\nitem is on or off at a step, or for every step of its workflow. Told,\nchecked and enforced go: an inferential rule is said to the agent, a\ndeterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. The\ncost is the old \"checked\" rules, which noted a break and let it pass;\nthey start off, so nothing changes until you turn one on.''','''A step's rules sort on three questions. Is it a constraint or a\ncapability? Is it feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts, or\nfeedback, which checks what it did? And does it come from the\nworkspace's repository or from Bastion? Each item is on or off at a step,\nor for every step of its workflow. Told, checked and enforced go: a\nfeedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and\na grant keeps ask or allowed. The cost is the old \"checked\" rules, which\nnoted a break and let it pass; they start off, so nothing changes until\nyou turn one on.''')\nhead=head.replace('''- A constraint's mode is inferential (stored as told) or deterministic\n  (stored as enforced). Migration 9 turns each checked one deterministic\n  and off for every workflow.''','''- A constraint is feedforward (stored as told) or feedback (stored as\n  enforced). A reviewer is feedback: it reads what the step did. Migration\n  9 turns each checked one into feedback, off for every workflow.''')\nhead=head.replace('''  workspace brings as inferential capabilities.''','''  workspace brings as feedforward capabilities.''')\nrest=s[i:]\nrest=rest.replace('''- Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into\n  inferential and deterministic, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every\n  row.\n- A Bastion constraint has an Inferential | Deterministic switch; going\n  deterministic asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask |\n  Allowed.''','''- Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into\n  feedforward and feedback, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every row.\n- A Bastion rule has a Feedforward | Feedback switch; going to feedback\n  asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask | Allowed.''')\nopen(p,'w').write(head+rest)\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| D56 |'); j=s.index('\\n',i)\ns=s[:i]+'''| D56 | A constraint or capability is feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts (a rule it is told, a skill, an agent, a note on what it may do), or feedback, which checks what it did (a word match, a hook, a review check, a reviewer); it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: a feedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"inferential\\|deterministic\" PLAN.md DECISIONS.md | head","description":"Rename the modes in the plan and D56"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3581,"cache_read_input_tokens":874195,"output_tokens":1860,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":571},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3581,"eph