{"parentUuid":"1c39eaa4-7b85-4d3f-a9e0-07cad92579af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyciMFgNodEwG5rxE1Tw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bastion now enforces the charter, with a new Workspaces page showing it. I'll write the plan across three pages (Constraints, Capabilities, Permissions) and build those first.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":945371,"output_tokens":2912,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1942},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1723,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2912,"cache_read_input_tokens":945371,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1723},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"26ccefae-db0d-4c4d-8987-ff3a009d1e4a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyciLnQip1hnxufMCLoD","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e8b2b74-aafb-415f-b195-89051a34c09b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:51:49.918Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"9e8b2b74-aafb-415f-b195-89051a34c09b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyciMFgNodEwG5rxE1Tw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AmDQkPNujx3SL2jHUvqwhS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('### R2.'); j=s.index('## Open questions')\ns=s[:i]+'''### R2. Rules by type and mode (checkpoint)\n\n- Done as a checkpoint on the Workflows page (2d44301): feedforward and\n  feedback, Workspace and Bastion chips, a Feedforward | Feedback switch,\n  and an Add bar. P1 to P3 move it to pages of its own.\n\n### P1. Three rules pages (D57)\n\n- Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions return to the top bar.\n  Constraints holds rules, checks, hooks and reviewers; Capabilities the\n  notes on what the agent may use; Permissions the grants, ask or allowed.\n- Each page has two views. Global sets an item on or off for every\n  workflow. Workflows opens an item's list of workflows and their steps,\n  each Inherit | On | Off, so a rule lands on the steps you pick.\n\n### P2. A Workspaces page\n\n- Each workspace's charter, read-only: AGENTS.md, its permissions and\n  hooks, its skills and agents. Bastion still applies the charter; it\n  leaves the rules pages because it changes in the repository.\n\n### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change\n\n- The workflow level's rules panel goes. A step's Rules tab lists what\n  applies at it, read-only, with a link to each page.\n- VISION.md and DECISIONS.md say where rules live.\n\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| D56 |'); j=s.index('\\n',i)+1\ns=s[:j]+'''| D57 | Rules live on three pages, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions, each with a Global view and a Workflows view that picks the workflows and steps an item applies to. A step lists what applies at it, read-only. The charter shows on a Workspaces page; Bastion still applies it, but it is not edited with Bastion's rules. This replaces D53's \"no Constraints or Capabilities page\". |\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit show HEAD~25:crates/bastion-desktop/src/icons.rs 2>/dev/null | grep -n \"CONSTRAINTS\\|CAPABILITIES\" | head -3 || true; git log --oneline -1 --format=%h -S\"pub const CONSTRAINTS\" -- crates/bastion-desktop/src/icons.rs","description":"Write the P1 to P3 plan and D57, find the old icons"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":945371,"output_tokens":2912,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1942},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1723,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2912,"cache_read_input_tokens":945371,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1723},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AmDQkPNujx3SL2jHUvqwhS":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('### R2.'); j=s.index('## Open questions')\ns=s[:i]+'''### R2. Rules by type and mode (checkpoint)\n\n- Done as a checkpoint on the Workflows page (2d44301): feedforward and\n  feedback, Workspace and Bastion chips, a Feedforward | Feedback switch,\n  and an Add bar. P1 to P3 move it to pages of its own.\n\n### P1. Three rules pages (D57)\n\n- Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions return to the top bar.\n  Constraints holds rules, checks, hooks and reviewers; Capabilities the\n  notes on what the agent may use; Permissions the grants, ask or allowed.\n- Each page has two views. Global sets an item on or off for every\n  workflow. Workflows opens an item's list of workflows and their steps,\n  each Inherit | On | Off, so a rule lands on the steps you pick.\n\n### P2. A Workspaces page\n\n- Each workspace's charter, read-only: AGENTS.md, its permissions and\n  hooks, its skills and agents. Bastion still applies the charter; it\n  leaves the rules pages because it changes in the repository.\n\n### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change\n\n- The workflow level's rules panel goes. A step's Rules tab lists what\n  applies at it, read-only, with a link to each page.\n- VISION.md and DECISIONS.md say where rules live.\n\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| D56 |'); j=s.index('\\n',i)+1\ns=s[:j]+'''| D57 | Rules live on three pages, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions, each with a Global view and a Workflows view that picks the workflows and steps an item applies to. A step lists what applies at it, read-only. The charter shows on a Workspaces page; Bastion still applies it, but it is not edited with Bastion's rules. This replaces D53's \"no Constraints or Capabilities page\". |\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit show HEAD~25:crates/bastion-desktop/src/icons.rs 2>/dev/null | grep -n \"CONSTRAINTS\\|CAPABILITIES\" | head -3 || true; git log --oneline -1 --format=%h -S\"pub const CONSTRAINTS\" -- crates/bastion-desktop/src/icons.rs","description":"Write the P1 to P3 plan and D57, find the old icons"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01AmDQkPNujx3SL2jHUvqwhS":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"26ccefae-db0d-4c4d-8987-ff3a009d1e4a","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgyciLnQip1hnxufMCLoD","type":"assistant","uuid":"fdc5bd82-51f2-4a3a-a9c1-5570cac942f7","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:51:57.195Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"c