{"parentUuid":"fdc5bd82-51f2-4a3a-a9c1-5570cac942f7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"37211818-95a6-4835-b720-c9efefd2895a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AmDQkPNujx3SL2jHUvqwhS","type":"tool_result","content":"9:pub const CONSTRAINTS: &str = r#\"<path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z\"/><path d=\"m9 12 2 2 4-4\"/>\"#;\n10:pub const CAPABILITIES: &str = r#\"<path d=\"M2.586 17.414A2 2 0 0 0 2 18.828V21a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h3a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h1a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h.172a2 2 0 0 0 1.414-.586l.814-.814a6.5 6.5 0 1 0-4-4z\"/><circle cx=\"16.5\" cy=\"7.5\" r=\".5\" fill=\"black\"/>\"#;\nddbaaef","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d22b918d-15b4-426d-921b-495dabbd40a0","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:51:57.717Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"9:pub const CONSTRAINTS: &str = r#\"<path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z\"/><path d=\"m9 12 2 2 4-4\"/>\"#;\n10:pub const CAPABILITIES: &str = r#\"<path d=\"M2.586 17.414A2 2 0 0 0 2 18.828V21a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h3a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h1a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h.172a2 2 0 0 0 1.414-.586l.814-.814a6.5 6.5 0 1 0-4-4z\"/><circle cx=\"16.5\" cy=\"7.5\" r=\".5\" fill=\"black\"/>\"#;\nddbaaef","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":83,"oldLines":6,"newStart":83,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D54 | A constraint or a grant is one item that three scopes turn on or off: all workflows (`*`), one workflow, and one step, each with `!` for off. The most specific setting wins. A list with no `*` means every step when it turns no step on, and only the steps it names otherwise. A grant is an item for one kind and one function; a step turns items on or off rather than replacing its kind's grants, which replaces D48's \"take the place of\". A rung belongs to the item, not to a scope. |"," | D55 | A constraint is judged by an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or by code (a word match, a hook, a review check). Promoting a told rule gives it a deterministic form; demoting keeps the form and stops running it. |"," | D56 | A constraint or capability is feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts (a rule it is told, a skill, an agent, a note on what it may do), or feedback, which checks what it did (a word match, a hook, a review check, a reviewer); it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: a feedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |","+| D57 | Rules live on three pages, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions, each with a Global view and a Workflows view that picks the workflows and steps an item applies to. A step lists what applies at it, read-only. The charter shows on a Workspaces page; Bastion still applies it, but it is not edited with Bastion's rules. This replaces D53's \"no Constraints or Capabilities page\". |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":37,"oldLines":19,"newStart":37,"newLines":32,"lines":[" `!*`. The charter listing shows demo-local's agent `strict`. The brief"," lists \"You may\" before its rules."," ","-### R2. The rules view by type and mode","+### R2. Rules by type and mode (checkpoint)"," ","-- Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into","-  feedforward and feedback, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every row.","-- A Bastion rule has a Feedforward | Feedback switch; going to feedback","-  asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask | Allowed.","-- The levels are the workflow and the step. What applies to every","-  workflow shows as inherited at the workflow; editing it for all","-  workflows waits.","+- Done as a checkpoint on the Workflows page (2d44301): feedforward and","+  feedback, Workspace and Bastion chips, a Feedforward | Feedback switch,","+  and an Add bar. P1 to P3 move it to pages of its own."," ","-### R3. Docs","+### P1. Three rules pages (D57)"," ","-- VISION.md and DECISIONS.md say how rules sort.","+- Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions return to the top bar.","+  Constraints holds rules, checks, hooks and reviewers; Capabilities the","+  notes on what the agent may use; Permissions the grants, ask or allowed.","+- Each page has two views. Global sets an item on or off for every","+  workflow. Workflows opens an item's list of workflows and their steps,","+  each Inherit | On | Off, so a rule lands on the steps you pick.","+","+### P2. A Workspaces page","+","+- Each workspace's charter, read-only: AGENTS.md, its permissions and","+  hooks, its skills and agents. Bastion still applies the charter; it","+  leaves the rules pages because it changes in the repository.","+","+### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change","+","+- The workflow level's rules panel goes. A step's Rules tab lists what","+  applies at it, read-only, with a link to each page.","+- VISION.md and DECISIONS.md say where rules live."," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"26ccefae-db0d-4c4d-8987-ff3a009d1e4a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remot