n branch (you will usually use this for PRs): main\n\nGit user: Ian Johnson\n\nStatus:\nM DECISIONS.md\n M PLAN.md\n M crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules/constraints.rs\n M crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules/layers.rs\n M crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules/mod.rs\n?? crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules/applies.rs\n?? crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules/pages.rs\n\nRecent commits:\n2d44301 R2 (checkpoint): rules by type and mode, at a workflow and its steps\n5ef98f9 R1: feedforward and feedback on the server (D56)\n0917c1c G3: one rule, two forms (D55)\nd7db219 G2: rules at three levels on the Workflows page\ndbc3f40 G1: rules and grants at three scopes (D54)\n\nClaude Code attached this context automatically; it isn't part of the user's message. It describes the user's own account and workspace, so they don't need it reported back.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
