{"parentUuid":"00cad7a9-70d2-409a-aba5-9809a8657bcb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"37211818-95a6-4835-b720-c9efefd2895a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ka7x6AbFNwNCFUnptHn2GC","type":"tool_result","content":"19:## Phases\n24:### R1. The model on the server (D56)\n40:### R2. Rules by type and mode (checkpoint)\n44:  and an Add bar. P1 to P3 move it to pages of its own.\n46:### P1. Three rules pages (D57)\n55:### P2. A Workspaces page\n61:### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change\n67:## Open questions\n69:- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a bundle of the above (an\n86:| D57 | Rules live on three pages, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions, each with a Global view and a Workflows view that picks the workflows and steps an item applies to. A step lists what applies at it, read-only. The charter shows on a Workspaces page; Bastion still applies it, but it is not edited with Bastion's rules. This replaces D53's \"no Constraints or Capabilities page\". |\n87-\n88-## Open questions\n89-\n90-- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's\n91-  dark dial can run to merge. Should merge always need a person, or a machine\n92-  verdict, such as the `verify.yaml` contract?\n93-- **Configuration in git.** ghola keeps configuration in files under review;\n94-  Bastion keeps it in the database with versions (D26). Should rules also be\n95-  importable as files, such as team rule packs shared by servers?\n96-- **Multi-user hosting.** A shared server with people and TLS works today.\n97-  Is hosted Bastion a goal?\n98-- **Unused engine workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's\n23:- **Its rules:** the constraints its agent works under, and the calls the\n30:text filled in, and you can change every step of them.\n45:## Two levels: each server, and all of them\n58:step, and what applies at every step shows there when you pick no step. A\n74:  enforced. They apply at one workflow step, or at every step.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3e820324-b3e0-4298-abbc-ce2b17e2600f","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:01:19.054Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"19:## Phases\n24:### R1. The model on the server (D56)\n40:### R2. Rules by type and mode (checkpoint)\n44:  and an Add bar. P1 to P3 move it to pages of its own.\n46:### P1. Three rules pages (D57)\n55:### P2. A Workspaces page\n61:### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change\n67:## Open questions\n69:- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a bundle of the above (an\n86:| D57 | Rules live on three pages, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions, each with a Global view and a Workflows view that picks the workflows and steps an item applies to. A step lists what applies at it, read-only. The charter shows on a Workspaces page; Bastion still applies it, but it is not edited with Bastion's rules. This replaces D53's \"no Constraints or Capabilities page\". |\n87-\n88-## Open questions\n89-\n90-- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's\n91-  dark dial can run to merge. Should merge always need a person, or a machine\n92-  verdict, such as the `verify.yaml` contract?\n93-- **Configuration in git.** ghola keeps configuration in files under review;\n94-  Bastion keeps it in the database with versions (D26). Should rules also be\n95-  importable as files, such as team rule packs shared by servers?\n96-- **Multi-user hosting.** A shared server with people and TLS works today.\n97-  Is hosted Bastion a goal?\n98-- **Unused engine workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's\n23:- **Its rules:** the constraints its agent works under, and the calls the\n30:text filled in, and you can change every step of them.\n45:## Two levels: each server, and all of them\n58:step, and what applies at every step shows there when you pick no step. A\n74:  enforced. They apply at one workflow step, or at every step.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":fa