{"parentUuid":"ee6415ba-3c92-4ffd-bffd-8948435bc666","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgydU4temdNwwBn94NVmQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T5AiZbeGrdGvDdy9cbUqcj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nv=open('VISION.md').read()\na=\"\"\"**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Engine and Settings belong to\nthe server you pick. A step's rules live on the Workflows page, with the\nstep, and what applies at every step shows there when you pick no step. A\nrules page never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only\nits own jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing.\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,\nPermissions, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. Bastion\nholds the rules as its harness, and a workflow applies them: each rules\npage turns an item on for every workflow, or for the workflows and steps\nyou pick. A step's Rules tab lists what applies there, read-only. A rules\npage never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only its\nown jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing.\"\"\"\nassert a in v; v=v.replace(a,b)\na=\"\"\"- **Rules, by layer:** the charter each workspace's repository brings; the\n  harness, what an agent may call and the rules and hooks on those calls;\n  and the factory, the checks on the work and the reviewers that must pass.\n  Each grant is ask or allowed, and each constraint runs from told to\n  enforced. They apply at one workflow step, or at every step.\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"- **Rules:** constraints, what the agent must keep; capabilities, what it\n  may use; and permissions, what the gate lets a call do. A constraint is\n  feedforward, told to the agent before it acts, or feedback, a check, hook\n  or reviewer on what it did. Each grant is ask or allowed. Each item\n  applies at every workflow, or at the workflows and steps you pick. The\n  charter each workspace's repository brings applies too, and changes in\n  the repository.\"\"\"\nassert a in v; v=v.replace(a,b)\nopen('VISION.md','w').write(v)\np=open('PLAN.md').read()\np=p.replace(\"### P1. Three rules pages (D57)\\n\",\"### P1. Three rules pages (D57), done\\n\")\np=p.replace(\"### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change\\n\",\"### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change, done\\n\")\nopen('PLAN.md','w').write(p)\nEOF\ncargo fmt --all -- --check && scripts/check-seams.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 && CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A6 | head; CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test --workspace 2>&1 | grep -cE \"FAILED|panicked|[1-9][0-9]* failed\"","description":"Update docs and run CI","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1102,"cache_read_input_tokens":200496,"output_tokens":1136,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":83},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1102,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1136,"cache_read_input_tokens":200496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1102,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1102},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01T5AiZbeGrdGvDdy9cbUqcj":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\nv=open('VISION.md').read()\na=\"\"\"**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Engine and Settings belong to\nthe server you pick. A step's rules live on the Workflows page, with the\nstep, and what applies at every step shows there when you pick no step. A\nrules page never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only\nits own jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing.\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,\nPermissions, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. Bastion\nholds the rules as its harness, and a workflow applies them: each rules\npage turns an item on for every workflow, or for the workflows and steps\nyou pick. A step's Rules tab lists what applies there, read-only. A rules\npage never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only its\nown jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing.\"\"\"\nassert a in v; v=v.replace(a,b)\na=\"\"\"- **Rules, by layer:** the charter each workspace's repository brings; the\n  harness, what an agent may call and the rules and hooks on those calls;\n  and the factory, the checks on the work and the reviewers that must pass.\n  Each grant is ask or allowed, and each constraint runs from told to\n  enforced. They apply at one workflow step, or at every step.\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"- **Rules:** constraints, what the agent must keep; capabilities, what it\n  may use; and permissions, what the gate lets a call do. A constraint is\n  feedforward, told to the agent before it acts, or feedback, a check, hook\n  or reviewer on what it did. Each grant is ask or allowed. Each item\n  applies at every workflow, or at the workflows and steps you pick. The\n  charter each workspace's repository brings applies too, and changes in\n  the repository.\"\"\"\nassert a in v; v=v.replace(a,b)\nopen('VISION.md','w').write(v)\np=open('PLAN.md').read()\np=p.replace(\"### P1. Three rules pages (D57)\\n\",\"### P1. Three rules pages (D57), done\\n\")\np=p.replace(\"### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change\\n\",\"### P3. The Workflows page shows, the pages change, done\\n\")\nopen('PLAN.md','w').write(p)\nEOF\ncargo fmt --all -- --check && scripts/check-seams.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 && CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy --workspace -