{"parentUuid":"4dfa5ba4-120f-46f7-8c5a-182b7fd97b9c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"36ed1261-8c70-4389-a294-f02db2205827","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Let's take a step back and update the vision. Bastion is a control plane but functionally it is a harness and factory manager segregated by servers. I want to support things that other harnesses do, such as rules, agents, hooks, and so forth - many of these are already implemented\nI want to manage them in the app to be able to manage them, promote/demote them, easily enable/disable them.\nAdditional rules, agents, skills, and so forth may come in through a workspace's charter. That's fine - allow them to be used - they are project specific. I also want the ability to edit these as well in the UI. Don't allow for global rules, but make applying them to things easily, whether step, all steps in a workflow, mutliple workflows, or all workflows. None of these things should be global over workflows - I don't want any global settings in any way other than just selected to apply it to all workflows."},"uuid":"d6f335be-9caa-43c7-be3e-cc2cd950a2e7","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:09:13.778Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":191,"turnIndex":291},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
