{"parentUuid":"a090416b-3ab7-4df6-88b5-dbe4095f64d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyeFP7HppSYRTRWhfZWY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While the push runs, I rewrite the vision."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1983,"cache_read_input_tokens":205628,"output_tokens":3859,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2255},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1983,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3859,"cache_read_input_tokens":205628,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1983},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f9b21e7f-cf35-4794-9877-52563bd4e8b8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyeFNsPbGVE5P7a4GE7o","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4e0797c-9e0f-44ee-9a58-d206fbdafd6c","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:12:00.877Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"e4e0797c-9e0f-44ee-9a58-d206fbdafd6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyeFP7HppSYRTRWhfZWY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017cyYWngt372SeL378Ltd3L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nv=open('VISION.md').read()\ndef sub(a,b):\n    global v\n    assert a in v, a[:50]; v=v.replace(a,b)\nsub(\"\"\"Bastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,\nand Bastion fulfills each request as a job: agents work through the\nworkflow's steps, under the rules you set on each step. Jobs and workflows\nare the two ideas everything else serves. The cost is plain: a job does only\nwhat its workflow says, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone.\nBastion runs on your machine, on a remote server, or on both at once.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Bastion is an agent control plane. On each server, it manages a harness and\na factory: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent works under,\nand the workflows that run it. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a\njob through a workflow. The cost is plain: a job does only what its workflow\nsays, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone. Bastion runs on your\nmachine, on a remote server, or on both.\"\"\")\ni=v.index(\"## Rules move onto the workflow\"); j=v.index(\"## Two levels\")\nv=v[:i]+\"\"\"## The harness and the factory\n\nOther agent harnesses keep rules, agents, skills and hooks in files.\nBastion keeps the same items on the server, and many of them already work:\nrules, checks, hooks, reviewers, notes and grants. You manage each one in\nthe app:\n\n- **Promote or demote it.** A rule moves between feedforward, told to the\n  agent before it acts, and feedback, a check, hook or reviewer that judges\n  what the agent did. A grant moves between ask and allowed.\n- **Turn it on or off.** One switch, and the item stays as it is.\n- **Apply it.** Select one step, every step of a workflow, some workflows,\n  or all workflows.\n\nNothing is global. \"All workflows\" is a selection, the same as one step,\nand an item applies only where you selected it. An item with no selection\napplies nowhere. So a step's Rules tab shows everything that applies at it,\nand nothing applies from somewhere you can't see.\n\n## A workspace's charter\n\nA repository can bring its own items in its charter: `AGENTS.md` and\n`.agents/`, with its rules, agents, skills and hooks. These items belong to\nthe project, so they apply only to jobs in that workspace. A step can use\nthem, and you read and edit them in the app the same way as Bastion's own.\nAn edit in the app changes the file in the repository. An agent's turn may\nread the charter but may not change it.\n\n\"\"\"+v[j:]\nsub(\"\"\"**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,\nPermissions, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. Bastion\nholds the rules as its harness, and a workflow applies them: each rules\npage turns an item on for every workflow, or for the workflows and steps\nyou pick. A step's Rules tab lists what applies there, read-only. A rules\npage never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only its\nown jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,\nPermissions, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. Each rules\npage applies an item to the steps and workflows you select, and a step's\nRules tab lists what applies there. A rules page never mixes two servers,\nbecause each server's rules shape only its own jobs, and a sum of two rule\nsets means nothing.\"\"\")\nsub(\"\"\"- **Rules:** constraints, what the agent must keep; capabilities, what it\n  may use; and permissions, what the gate lets a call do. A constraint is\n  feedforward, told to the agent before it acts, or feedback, a check, hook\n  or reviewer on what it did. Each grant is ask or allowed. Each item\n  applies at every workflow, or at the workflows and steps you pick. The\n  charter each workspace's repository brings applies too, and changes in\n  the repository.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Its harness and factory:** constraints, what the agent must keep;\n  capabilities, what it may use; and permissions, what the gate lets a\n  call do. Each item applies only where you selected it. A workspace's\n  charter adds its own items, for that workspace's jobs.\"\"\")\nopen('VISION.md','w').write(v)\nEOF\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py VISION.md 2>&1 | tail -25","description":"Rewrite vision sections, run voice-check"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1983,"cache_read_input_tokens":205628,"output_tokens":3859,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2255},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1983,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3859,"cache_read_input_tokens":205628,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1983},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017cyYWngt372SeL378Ltd3L":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\nv=open('VISION.md').read()\ndef sub(a,b):\n    global v\n    assert a in v, a[:50]; v=v.replace(a,b)\nsub(\"\"\"Bastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,\nand Bastion fulfills each request as a job: agents work through the\nworkflow's steps, under the rules you set on each step. Jobs and workflows\nare the two ideas everything else serves. The cost is plain: a job does only\nwhat its workflow says, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone.\nBastion runs on your machine, on a remote server, or on both at once.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Bastion is an agent control plane. On each server, it manages a harness and\na factory: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent works under,\nand the workflows that run it. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a\njob through a workflow. The cost is plain: a job does only what its workflow\nsays, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone. Bastion runs on your\nmachine, on a remote server, or on both.\"\"\")\ni=v.index(\"## Rules move onto the workflow\"); j=v.index(\"## Two levels\")\nv=v[:i]+\"\"\"## The harness and the factory\n\nOther agent harnesses keep rules, agents, skills and hooks in files.\nBastion keeps the same items on the server, and many of them already work:\nrules, checks, hooks, reviewers, notes and grants. You manage each one in\nthe app:\n\n- **Promote or demote it.** A rule moves between feedforward, told to the\n  agent before it acts, and feedback, a check, hook or reviewer that judges\n  what the agent did. A grant moves between ask and allowed.\n- **Turn it on or off.** One switch, and the item stays as it is.\n- **Apply it.** Select one step, every step of a workflow, some workflows,\n  or all workflows.\n\nNothing is global. \"All workflows\" is a selection, the same as one step,\nand an item applies only where you selected it. An item with no selection\napplies nowhere. So a step's Rules tab shows everything that applies at it,\nand nothing applies from somewhere you can't see.\n\n## A workspace's charter\n\nA repository can bring its own items in its charter: `AGENTS.md` and\n`.agents/`, with its rules, agents, skills and hooks. These items belong to\nthe project, so they apply only to jobs in that workspace. A step can use\nthem, and you read and edit them in the app the same way as Bastion's own.\nAn edit in the app changes the file in the repository. An agent's turn may\nread the charter but may not change it.\n\n\"\"\"+v[j:]\nsub(\"\"\"**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,\nPermissions, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. Bastion\nholds the rules as its harness, and a workflow applies them: each rules\npage turns an item on for every workflow, or for the workflows and steps\nyou pick. A step's Rules tab lists what applies there, read-only. A rules\npage never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only its\nown jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,\nPermissions, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. Each rules\npage applies an item to the steps and workflows you select, and a step's\nRules tab lists what applies there. A rules page never mixes two servers,\nbecause each server's rules shape only its own jobs, and a sum of two rule\nsets means nothing.\"\"\")\nsub(\"\"\"- **Rules:** constraints, what the agent must keep; capabilities, what it\n  may use; and permissions, what the gate lets a call do. A constraint is\n  feedforward, told to the agent before it acts, or feedback, a check, hook\n  or reviewer on what it did. Each grant is ask or allowed. Each item\n  applies at every workflow, or at the workflows and steps you pick. The\n  charter each workspace's repository brings applies too, and changes in\n  the repository.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Its harness and factory:** constraints, what the agent must keep;\n  capabilities, what it may use; and permissions, what the gate lets a\n  call do. Each item applies only where you selected it. A workspace's\n  charter adds its own items, for that workspace's jobs.\"\"\")\nopen('VISION.md','w').write(v)\nEOF\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py VISION.md 2>&1 | tail -25","description":"Rewrite vision sections, run voice-check"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_017cyYWngt372SeL378Ltd3L":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bast