{"parentUuid":"7d9a4153-940a-4e15-a8b9-78c8b839f8d1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"50f3cf6a-f18b-4b70-b233-30aa8facc040","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017cyYWngt372SeL378Ltd3L","type":"tool_result","content":"VISION [informational/ste]  (1044 words, 2 findings)\n  - tic triad: 5 (budget 2) [advisory: data lists of three are fine, only rhetorical triads count]\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it\n\n2 findings across 1 page(s)\nchain: voicecheck -> /humanizer (tone) -> /slopbeth (slop) -> voicecheck (gate)\nno later stage may reintroduce a finding above","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"746d6562-da0e-4e47-9b42-23066196664b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:12:12.187Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"VISION [informational/ste]  (1044 words, 2 findings)\n  - tic triad: 5 (budget 2) [advisory: data lists of three are fine, only rhetorical triads count]\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it\n\n2 findings across 1 page(s)\nchain: voicecheck -> /humanizer (tone) -> /slopbeth (slop) -> voicecheck (gate)\nno later stage may reintroduce a finding above","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":12,"newStart":3,"newLines":12,"lines":[" <!-- voice-register: informational -->"," <!-- voice-english: ste -->"," ","-Bastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,","-and Bastion fulfills each request as a job: agents work through the","-workflow's steps, under the rules you set on each step. Jobs and workflows","-are the two ideas everything else serves. The cost is plain: a job does only","-what its workflow says, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone.","-Bastion runs on your machine, on a remote server, or on both at once.","+Bastion is an agent control plane. On each server, it manages a harness and","+a factory: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent works under,","+and the workflows that run it. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a","+job through a workflow. The cost is plain: a job does only what its workflow","+says, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone. Bastion runs on your","+machine, on a remote server, or on both."," "," ## Jobs and workflows"," "]},{"oldStart":29,"oldLines":18,"newStart":29,"newLines":33,"lines":[" ready, merged or left for you. Bastion ships the common workflows with their"," text filled in, and you can change every step of them."," ","-## Rules move onto the workflow","+## The harness and the factory"," ","-Bastion used to split its rules into two layers. The harness bound an","-agent's calls. The factory bound the work around them: what a step may do,","-and when a change lands. Both now live more and more on a workflow and its","-steps, and Bastion applies them as each step runs. I think the two layers","-will collapse into one, with Bastion applying whatever the workflow and its","-steps set. The split may still be useful, though, and that isn't settled;","-the next few workflows people write will settle it.","+Other agent harnesses keep rules, agents, skills and hooks in files.","+Bastion keeps the same items on the server, and many of them already work:","+rules, checks, hooks, reviewers, notes and grants. You manage each one in","+the app:"," ","-A repository brings its own rules too: its charter, in `AGENTS.md` and","-`.agents/settings.json`. A turn may read the charter but may not change it.","+- **Promote or demote it.** A rule moves between feedforward, told to the","+  agent before it acts, and feedback, a check, hook or reviewer that judges","+  what the agent did. A grant moves between ask and allowed.","+- **Turn it on or off.** One switch, and the item stays as it is.","+- **Apply it.** Select one step, every step of a workflow, some workflows,","+  or all workflows.","+","+Nothing is global. \"All workflows\" is a selection, the same as one step,","+and an item applies only where you selected it. An item with no selection","+applies nowhere. So a step's Rules tab shows everything that applies at it,","+and nothing applies from somewhere you can't see.","+","+## A workspace's charter","+","+A repository can bring its own items in its charter: `AGENTS.md` and","+`.agents/`, with its rules, agents, skills and hooks. These items belong to","+the project, so they apply only to jobs in that workspace. A step can use","+them, and you read and edit them in the app the same way as Bastion's own.","+An edit in the app changes the file in the repository. An agent's turn may","+read the charter but may not change it."," "," ## Two levels: each server, and all of them"," "]},{"oldStart":54,"oldLines":12,"newStart":69,"newLines":11,"lines":[" on it wherever it lives."," "," **Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,","-Permissions, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. Bastion","-holds the rules as its harness, and a workflow applies them: each rules","-page turns an item on for every workflow, or for the workflows and steps","-you pick. A step's Rules tab lists what applies there, read-only. A rules","-page never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only its","-own jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing.","+Permissions, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. Each rules","+page applies an item to the steps and workflows you select, and a step's","+Rules tab lists what applies there. A rules page never mixes two servers,","+because each server's rules shape only its own jobs, and a sum of two rule","+sets means nothing."," "," ## What a server holds"," "]},{"oldStart":69,"oldLines":13,"newStart":83,"newLines":10,"lines":[" - **Workspaces:** the repositories it works in, each with its checks, its","   setup, its VM image, and what happens to a job's branch at the end."," - **Workflows:** its series of steps, each step with its settings.","-- **Rules:** constraints, what the agent must keep; capabilities, what it","-  may use; and permissions, what the gate lets a call do. A constraint is","-  feedforward, told to the agent before it acts, or feedback, a check, hook","-  or reviewer on what it did. Each grant is ask or allowed. Each item","-  applies at every workflow, or at the workflows and steps you pick. The","-  charter each workspace's repository brings applies too, and changes in","-  the repository.","+- **Its harness and factory:** constraints, what the agent must keep;","+  capabilities, what it may use; and permissions, what the gate lets a","+  call do. Each item applies only where you selected it. A workspace's","+  charter adds its own items, for that workspace's jobs."," - **Settings:** its model providers, its people and their roles, its","   notifications, and its secrets."," - **Records:** its jobs, its audit log, its evals, its costs, and what"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f9b21e7f-cf35-4794-9877-52563bd4e8b8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7d9a4153-940a-4e15-a8b9-78c8b839f8d1","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
