{"parentUuid":"14b6d5fd-09c4-47ca-adf9-5ceff7719d9a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01CAJ98Ms9U1UrZDVtZvQKrn","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":62},"type":"attachment","uuid":"de5ef395-2771-4dfd-9ff0-77b8ee0fa421","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:13:51.311Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"14b6d5fd-09c4-47ca-adf9-5ceff7719d9a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3a8b9318-9b4b-4fdb-a263-6f255f398c04","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CAJ98Ms9U1UrZDVtZvQKrn","type":"tool_result","content":"# Bastion plan: rules by who judges them\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nA step's rules sort on three questions. Is it a constraint or a\ncapability? Is it feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts, or\nfeedback, which checks what it did? And does it come from the\nworkspace's repository or from Bastion? Each item is on or off at a step,\nor for every step of its workflow. Told, checked and enforced go: a\nfeedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and\na grant keeps ask or allowed. The cost is the old \"checked\" rules, which\nnoted a break and let it pass; they start off, so nothing changes until\nyou turn one on.\n\nThe scopes plan (G1 to G3) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions\nare in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 to D56.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit\nbefore the next one starts.\n\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a bundle of the above (an\n  agent, its skills, its hooks and its MCP servers) that a step takes as\n  one?\n- **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use\n  a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?\n- **Rules for every workflow.** Whether some items should be set once for\n  all workflows, and where that lives.\n- **Codified and ambient context.** Constraints and direction are codified\n  context: written down, stable, and Bastion can scope and judge them.\n  Ambient context comes from MCP servers and other outside sources: it is\n  scattered, it changes over time, and it depends on state. How should\n  Bastion handle it: where it came from, how fresh it is, and when to read\n  it again? Today an MCP server is only a grant.\n121:pub const EVERY: &str = \"*\";\n124:pub fn setting(scopes: &[String], key: &str) -> Option<bool> {\n138:pub fn on_at(scopes: &[String], step: &str) -> bool {\n142:    set.or_else(|| setting(scopes, EVERY))\n154:pub fn set_scope(scopes: &mut Vec<String>, key: &str, on: Option<bool>) {\n155:    if key != EVERY && setting(scopes, EVERY).is_none() {\n157:        set_scope(scopes, EVERY, Some(every));\n283:pub fn fold(grants: &[Capability]) -> (Vec<Capability>, Vec<Capability>) {\n294:            set_scope(&mut items.last_mut().unwrap().scopes, EVERY, Some(false));\n815:        set_scope(&mut list, EVERY, Some(false));","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c6dda6a1-db65-4667-8026-36ffb0ee60e3","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:13:51.432Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Bastion plan: rules by who judges them\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nA step's rules sort on three questions. Is it a constraint or a\ncapability? Is it feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts, or\nfeedback, which checks what it did? And does it come from the\nworkspace's repository or from Bastion? Each item is on or off at a step,\nor for every step of its workflow. Told, checked and enforced go: a\nfeedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and\na grant keeps ask or allowed. The cost is the old \"checked\" rules, which\nnoted a break and let it pass; they start off, so nothing changes until\nyou turn one on.\n\nThe scopes plan (G1 to G3) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions\nare in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 to D56.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit\nbefore the next one starts.\n\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a bundle of the above (an\n  agent, its skills, its hooks and its MCP servers) that a step takes as\n  one?\n- **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use\n  a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?\n- **Rules for every workflow.** Whether some items should be set once for\n  all workflows, and where that lives.\n- **Codified and ambient context.** Constraints and direction are codified\n  context: written down, stable, and Bastion can scope and judge them.\n  Ambient context comes from MCP servers and other outside sources: it is\n  scattered, it changes over time, and it depends on state. How should\n  Bastion handle it: where it came from, how fresh it is, and when to read\n  it again? Today an MCP server is only a grant.\n121:pub const EVERY: &str = \"*\";\n124:pub fn setting(scopes: &[String], key: &str) -> Option<bool> {\n138:pub fn on_at(scopes: &[String], step: &str) -> bool {\n142:    set.or_else(|| setting(scopes, EVERY))\n154:pub fn set_scope(scopes: &mut Vec<String>, key: &str, on: Option<bool>) {\n155:    if key != EVERY && setting(scopes, EVERY).is_none() {\n157:        set_scope(scopes, EVERY, Some(every));\n283:pub fn fold(grants: &[Capability]) -> (Vec<Capability>, Vec<Capability>) {\n294:            set_scope(&mut items.last_mut().unwrap().scopes, EVERY, Some(false));\n815:        set_scope(&mut list, EVERY, Some(false));","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"89abe5e4-bc6a-4f26-a53c-90a79c2a2889","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"14b6d5fd-09c4-47ca-adf9-5ceff7719d9a","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"