{"parentUuid":"318141e4-49e1-4df6-ad63-5adb5ab5a986","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyekKqPiwRrhSUsmxvSZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing in the CLI or the workers creates items. I write the plan and the D58 addition, then do a live check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":250785,"output_tokens":1267,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":167},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":250785,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8fa3a546-a64b-462e-83ca-3afdcc7e2b23","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyekKZmwreDaBvF6tZge","type":"assistant","uuid":"f84bfff0-7283-472e-84d1-0e7086eb5605","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:18:12.552Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"f84bfff0-7283-472e-84d1-0e7086eb5605","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyekKqPiwRrhSUsmxvSZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UztrBtbwcK6eAXsArM8K6d","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Phases\")\nj=s.index(\"## Open questions\")\nhead='''# Bastion plan: nothing is global\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nBastion manages a harness and a factory on each server: rules, agents,\nskills, hooks, reviewers and grants. Each item applies only where you\nselect it: one step, a workflow's steps, some workflows, or all workflows\n(D58). A workspace's charter brings its own items for its jobs, and you\nedit them in the app; an edit is a commit on a branch, never on the base.\nEvery page shows all servers or one. The cost is the old default: a list\nthat selected nothing meant every step, so migration 10 writes that down\nas all workflows before the default turns off.\n\nThe rules-pages plan (R1, R2, P1, P3) is done, and git history holds it.\nDecisions are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 to D58.\n\n'''\nphases='''## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit\nbefore the next one starts.\n\n### S1. Nothing is global\n\n- An item with no selection applies nowhere, in core and in the desktop.\n  A narrower setting no longer writes down what all workflows had.\n- Migration 10 selects all workflows in each list that selected nothing,\n  so each item works as it did.\n- A new item made at all workflows carries `*`. A charter's rules and an\n  approved test carry `*` for their job's steps.\n- The Global view is named All workflows.\n\n### S2. The rules pages across all servers\n\n- On All servers, each rules page shows one section per server, named.\n- A change goes to its section's server.\n\n### S3. A Workspaces page\n\n- Each workspace and its charter: AGENTS.md, its permissions and hooks,\n  its skills and agents. All servers or one.\n\n### S4. Charter edits\n\n- Edit a charter file in the app. The server commits the edit on a new\n  branch of the workspace's repository, never on its base branch.\n- An agent's turn still may not change the charter.\n\n'''\ns=head+phases+s[j:]\ns=s.replace('''- **Rules for every workflow.** Whether some items should be set once for\n  all workflows, and where that lives.\n''','')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nd=open('DECISIONS.md').read()\na=\"A charter's items apply to their workspace's jobs, and the app edits them in the repository's files.\"\nassert a in d\nd=d.replace(a,\"A charter's items apply to their workspace's jobs, and the app edits them as a commit on a new branch of the workspace's repository, never on its base branch.\")\nopen('DECISIONS.md','w').write(d)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Rules for every\" PLAN.md; ps -o pid=,comm= -A | grep -i bastion","description":"Write plan, refine D58, list Bastion processes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":250785,"output_tokens":1267,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":167},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":250785,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UztrBtbwcK6eAXsArM8K6d":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Phases\")\nj=s.index(\"## Open questions\")\nhead='''# Bastion plan: nothing is global\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nBastion manages a harness and a factory on each server: rules, agents,\nskills, hooks, reviewers and grants. Each item applies only where you\nselect it: one step, a workflow's steps, some workflows, or all workflows\n(D58). A workspace's charter brings its own items for its jobs, and you\nedit them in the app; an edit is a commit on a branch, never on the base.\nEvery page shows all servers or one. The cost is the old default: a list\nthat selected nothing meant every step, so migration 10 writes that down\nas all workflows before the default turns off.\n\nThe rules-pages plan (R1, R2, P1, P3) is done, and git history holds it.\nDecisions are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 to D58.\n\n'''\nphases='''## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit\nbefore the next one starts.\n\n### S1. Nothing is global\n\n- An item with no selection applies nowhere, in core and in the desktop.\n  A narrower setting no longer writes down what all workflows had.\n- Migration 10 selects all workflows in each list that selected nothing,\n  so each item works as it did.\n- A new item made at all workflows carries `*`. A charter's rules and an\n  approved test carry `*` for their job's steps.\n- The Global view is named All workflows.\n\n### S2. The rules pages across all servers\n\n- On All servers, each rules page shows one section per server, named.\n- A change goes to its section's server.\n\n### S3. A Workspaces page\n\n- Each workspace and its charter: AGENTS.md, its permissions and hooks,\n  its skills and agents. All servers or one.\n\n### S4. Charter edits\n\n- Edit a charter file in the app. The server commits the edit on a new\n  branch of the workspace's repository, never on its base branch.\n- An agent's turn still may not change the charter.\n\n'''\ns=head+phases+s[j:]\ns=s.replace('''- **Rules for every workflow.** Whether some items should be set once for\n  all workflows, and where that lives.\n''','')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nd=open('DECISIONS.md').read()\na=\"A charter's items apply to their workspace's jobs, and the app edits them in the repository's files.\"\nassert a in d\nd=d.replace(a,\"A charter's items apply to their workspace's jobs, and the app edits them as a commit on a new branch of the workspace's repository, never on its base branch.\")\nopen('DECISIONS.md','w').write(d)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Rules for every\" PLAN.md; ps -o pid=,comm= -A | grep -i bastion","description":"Write plan, refine D58, list Bastion processes"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01UztrBtbwcK6eAXsArM8K6d":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8fa3a546-a64b-462e-83ca-3afdcc7e2b23","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgyekKZmwreDaBvF6tZge","type":"assistant","uuid":"78531d6f-518a-4572-97dd-09c2443eb111","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:18:20.962Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
