{"parentUuid":"889e28d5-f4b7-455d-b65e-ca61a9587f5e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyfrzydfyw67wYrrQ7cX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"S2 is committed as 549e5aa and not pushed. Workflows and Workspaces now hold the content from the other pages.\n\n- **Top bar:** Jobs, Workflows, Workspaces, Audit Log, Evals, Costs, Verification, Engine, Settings.\n- **Workflows:** It has the tabs Steps, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions. The rules pages are now those tabs, and they still have the All workflows and Workflows views.\n- **Workspaces:** It is a page with its own module, `pages/workspaces/`. Each workspace shows its name and Edit, then its path, checks and job limit, then its own charter: files, allows, rules, hooks, skills and agents. A workspace without a charter shows \"No charter.\" The add/edit form and the accounts moved here too.\n- **Settings:** As you asked, nothing about workspaces or charters is in Settings. Its servers card is now `settings/servers.rs`, and the rest is the same: people, providers, MCP servers, the factory, notifications and history.\n- **Checks:** CI and the safeguard pass. I checked the Workspaces page, the Steps tab and the Permissions tab in the app.\n\nTwo things I noticed, and I didn't change either:\n- **A default grant can now be removed.** The agent and skill `sandbox::*` grants show Remove, because migration 10 gave them only `*`. Remove deletes the grant on every workflow.\n- **The factory lines are still global settings.** \"Merge a finished job's branch\", \"Give a shell step the network\" and \"Send failing work back\" show on Permissions as server-wide values. That conflicts with D58. They could move to each workspace or each step.\n\nI stopped before S3 (all servers on Workflows and Workspaces) because only 1.3Gi of disk is left. Free about 4Gi and I'll continue."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":262,"cache_read_input_tokens":336414,"output_tokens":634,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":27},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":262,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":336414,"cache_creation_input_tokens":262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":262},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"497d876f-8741-4945-bb1f-68e3235a72a8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyfrzgGi3WbVvr68hgcN","type":"assistant","uuid":"8c1a1283-4c58-4a2f-8586-963eb3b55e7b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:32:53.138Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
